  "notes": "Official cause code and category were TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative discusses human performance/configuration control causal theme but no NRC cause code letter was assigned in the source fields, so cause node marked provisional per rule 4. Two reporting criteria cited (50.73(a)(2)(v)(D) and (a)(2)(i)(B)) both captured in reporting_basis and as REPORTED_UNDER edges. Isolation valve 2-FCV-074-0057 modeled as Component since it is discussed as part of the flow-diversion safety analysis directly relevant to this event's consequence assessment, not merely generic design context. No previous similar occurrence LER identified (narrative states none found in past three years) so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted. RHR Loop II SPS and DGs mentioned only in context of TS applicability windows, not as stated-operable backups during this specific inoperability window covering the full 3-year period, so no BACKED_UP_BY edges asserted for them; RHR system's heat removal function noted as available but this is a different function than SPS, so not modeled as a backup to the SPS consequence."
